Article 38 To establish a medical institution, the following conditions shall be met, and the procedures for approval or recordation shall be handled in accordance with relevant state regulations:
(1) Having a name, organizational structure, and premises that conform to regulations;
(2) Having funds, facilities, equipment, and medical and health personnel commensurate with the business to be carried out;
(3) Having corresponding rules and regulations;
(4) Being able to independently bear civil liability;
(5) Other conditions provided for by laws and administrative regulations.
A medical institution shall obtain a practice license according to law. It is prohibited to forge, alter, buy, sell, lease, or lend a medical institution's practice license.
The specific conditions and configurations of medical and health institutions at various levels and types shall conform to the standards for medical and health institutions formulated by the competent health department of the State Council.

Article 100 Where, in violation of the provisions of this Law, any of the following acts is committed, the health administrative department of the people's government at or above the county level shall order correction, confiscate illegal gains, and impose a fine of not less than two times but not more than ten times the illegal gains; if the illegal gains are less than 10,000 yuan, it shall be calculated as 10,000 yuan; the directly responsible supervisors and other directly responsible personnel shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) A government-run medical and health institution invests in establishing a medical and health institution without independent legal personality with other organizations;
(2) A medical and health institution leases or contracts out medical departments;
(3) A non-profit medical and health institution distributes or covertly distributes benefits to contributors or founders.

Article 102 Where, in violation of this Law, a medical and health personnel commits any of the following acts, the competent department of health and health of the people's government at or above the county level shall impose an administrative penalty in accordance with the provisions of laws and administrative regulations on the management of practicing physicians, nurses, and the prevention and handling of medical disputes:
(1) soliciting, illegally accepting property, or seeking other illegitimate benefits by taking advantage of his or her position;
(2) disclosing citizens' personal health information;
(3) failing to perform the obligation of disclosure in accordance with the provisions or violating medical ethics norms in the course of conducting medical research or providing medical and health services.
If the person specified in the preceding paragraph is a person in a medical and health institution run by the government, he or she shall be given a sanction according to law.
